A||||9||Master_Sushi||Oil in air intake :`( , few other little questions...||||7||
Z||000000||Master_Sushi||11-22-2001||05:44 PM||||I noticed that I have a little oil in my 84s air intake around the filter. Its not allot, just maybe a teaspoon amount. Not near enough to get into the TBI. Is this Blow by? Is my engine on its last legs?<P>Also looking into my oil filler, I can see everything looks pretty gunky and dirty even though I just changed the oil. Should I flush the engine with a cleaner? If so, I heard you can use 1 part auto trannie fluid and 1 part oil to do this. Is this a good idea or bad idea?<P>Can I clean out my K&N air filter out any way other then geting the recharge kit? I was thinking of throttle body cleaner or someting simmilar. The filter is geting pretty bad and I don't want to spend to much money! I'm a "bit" short on cash at the moment..... <P><BR>Thank ya! Happy thanks giving all!||||reg||7
Z||000001||Tigger||11-22-2001||06:20 PM||||I was getting oil in my aircleaner with my 84 SE for awhile after I bought it.  Replaced the PVC valve and breather, that helped a lot, then over time the oil disappeared.  I noticed after running high rpm's, the oil would show up.  Now with regular oil changes, the oil is gone.  My thinking is the oil passages that drain back out of the top of engine were semi plugged causing the oil to back up.<P>A compression check would let you know if the cause is from blow by.||||reg||1
Z||000002||REDHOTT88||11-22-2001||08:24 PM||||Not sure if this is the case, but my 88 Formula has a K&N air filter.<P>The filter is not disposable and when cleaned has to soaked with oil. (from K&N) Before replacing.<P>Sometimes the oil will ooze its way down and accumulate on bottom of air cleaner can. I just take it easy on the oil!<BR><P>------------------<BR>1988 Formula (red & shiny allover)- and she doesn't like to wear a bra!<BR>1st Place IMOMOC (In My Own Mind Of Course!)<BR>2nd Place IMWM (In My Wifes Mind!)||||reg||12
