Z||000008||CanadianGT||11-22-2001||11:17 PM||||I would check the PCV valve.  Take it off and shake it.  If you hear a rattle, then you know it is good.  If you dont,  replace it.  When there is problems on the outlet side of the PCV system, oil can get up into the aircleaner.  You could also use a manometer, and see if you PCV system is working properly<BR>PeAcE<BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000009||Master_Sushi||11-23-2001||01:39 AM||||Ok, I cleaned out my K&N air filter with some scrubbing and normal cleaners. Came out like new after 30 mins of working on it. Ya, its probably not filtering very well because I didn’t use the "special cleaning products", but its obviously leting in allot more air. An air filter isn’t exactly the most complex thing...<BR>Clean and Transparent = Good!<BR>Black Dirty and Opaque = BAD!<BR>I change my oil every 2k miles or so. I’m not to worried about it letting in dirty air. Removed air box restriction while I was at it also. Maybe with the clean filter and better airflow I gained a HP or two! Hey you never know   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. I can hear the engine through the intake now anyway, sounds manly   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P>I guess the oil in the filter isn’t to uncommon, I'll just check it every week or so to make sure things don’t get worse.<P>I see somebody started a thread about engine flushing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> ... hehe<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 11-23-2001).]||||reg||1
